  "structures": [],
  "explain": "Ischemic stroke is loss of blood supply to brain tissue. It results either from thrombosis (a clot forming in place on an atherosclerotic vessel) or embolism (a clot travelling from elsewhere, such as the heart in atrial fibrillation). Embolus: Greek embolos, plug or wedge. Thrombosis (e.g. atherosclerosis) and embolism (e.g. from atrial fibrillation).",
